.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dnsrecon
is a DNS enumeration and reconnaissance tool. It can:
.IP \(bu 2
Check all NS records for zone transfers (AXFR).
.IP \(bu 2
Enumerate general DNS records for a given domain (MX, SOA, NS, A, AAAA, SPF and TXT).
.IP \(bu 2
Perform common SRV record enumeration.
.IP \(bu 2
Perform top level domain (TLD) expansion.
.IP \(bu 2
Check for wildcard resolution.
.IP \(bu 2
Brute force subdomain and host A and AAAA records given a domain and a wordlist.
.IP \(bu 2
Perform PTR record lookups for a given IP range or CIDR.
.IP \(bu 2
Check a DNS server's cached records for A, AAAA and CNAME records given a list of host records (cache snooping).
.IP \(bu 2
Enumerate subdomains and hosts using Bing, Yandex and crt.sh.
.IP \(bu 2
Walk DNSSEC zones using NSEC records.
.IP \(bu 2
Expand netblocks found in SPF and WHOIS data using Shodan.
.PP
If no name server is given with
.BR \-n ,
the SOA server of the target domain is used.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show this help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR \fIDOMAIN\fR, \fB\-\-domain\fR \fIDOMAIN\fR
Target domain.
.TP
\fB\-iL\fR \fIINPUT_LIST\fR, \fB\-\-input\-list\fR \fIINPUT_LIST\fR
File containing a list of domains to perform DNS enumeration on, one per line.
.TP
\fB\-n\fR \fINS_SERVER\fR, \fB\-\-name_server\fR \fINS_SERVER\fR
Domain server to use. If none is given, the SOA of the target will be used. Multiple servers can be specified using a comma separated list.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR \fIRANGE\fR, \fB\-\-range\fR \fIRANGE\fR
IP range for reverse lookup brute force in formats (first-last) or in (range/bitmask).
.TP
\fB\-D\fR \fIDICTIONARY\fR, \fB\-\-dictionary\fR \fIDICTIONARY\fR
Dictionary file of subdomain and hostnames to use for brute force.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR
Filter out of brute force domain lookup, records that resolve to the wildcard defined IP address when saving records.
.TP
\fB\-a\fR
Perform AXFR with standard enumeration.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR
Perform a reverse lookup of IPv4 ranges in the SPF record with standard enumeration.
.TP
\fB\-b\fR
Perform Bing enumeration with standard enumeration.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR
Perform Yandex enumeration with standard enumeration.
.TP
\fB\-k\fR
Perform crt.sh enumeration with standard enumeration.
.TP
\fB\-w\fR
Perform deep whois record analysis and reverse lookup of IP ranges found through Whois when doing a standard enumeration.
.TP
\fB\-\-shodan\fR
Use Shodan to query netblocks discovered via SPF (\-s) and/or Whois (\-w) during standard enumeration.
.TP
\fB\-\-shodan\-active\fR
Actively validate Shodan-discovered names by resolving them and confirming they still match the queried netblock.
.TP
\fB\-\-shodan\-key\fR \fISHODAN_KEY\fR
Shodan API key. If omitted, SHODAN_API_KEY environment variable is used.
.TP
\fB\-z\fR
Performs a DNSSEC zone walk with standard enumeration.
.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR \fITHREADS\fR
Number of threads to use in reverse lookups, forward lookups, brute force and SRV record enumeration.
.TP
\fB\-\-lifetime\fR \fILIFETIME\fR
Time to wait for a server to respond to a query. default is 3.0.
.TP
\fB\-\-loglevel\fR \fILOGLEVEL\fR
Log level to use. default is INFO.
Possible values: \fBDEBUG\fR, \fBINFO\fR, \fBWARNING\fR, \fBERROR\fR, \fBCRITICAL\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\fR
Use TCP protocol to make queries.
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fIDB\fR
SQLite 3 file to save found records.
.TP
\fB\-x\fR \fIXML\fR, \fB\-\-xml\fR \fIXML\fR
XML file to save found records.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR \fICSV\fR, \fB\-\-csv\fR \fICSV\fR
Save output to a comma separated value file.
.TP
\fB\-j\fR \fIJSON\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR \fIJSON\fR
Save output to a JSON file.
.TP
\fB\-\-iw\fR
Continue brute forcing a domain even if a wildcard record is discovered.
.TP
\fB\-\-disable_check_nxdomain\fR
Disables check for NXDOMAIN hijacking on name servers.
.TP
\fB\-\-disable_check_recursion\fR
Disables check for recursion on name servers.
.TP
\fB\-\-disable_recurs\fR
Disable recursion desired flag in queries.
.TP
\fB\-\-disable_check_bindversion\fR
Disables check for BIND version on name servers.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
DNSrecon version.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbosity.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR \fITYPE\fR, \fB\-\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR
Type of enumeration to perform. Possible types:
.RS
.TP 10n
\fBstd\fR
SOA, NS, A, AAAA, MX and SRV.
.TP 10n
\fBrvl\fR
Reverse lookup of a given CIDR or IP range.
.TP 10n
\fBbrt\fR
Brute force domains and hosts using a given dictionary.
.TP 10n
\fBsrv\fR
SRV records.
.TP 10n
\fBaxfr\fR
Test all NS servers for a zone transfer.
.TP 10n
\fBbing\fR
Perform Bing search for subdomains and hosts.
.TP 10n
\fByand\fR
Perform Yandex search for subdomains and hosts.
.TP 10n
\fBcrt\fR
Perform crt.sh search for subdomains and hosts.
.TP 10n
\fBcaa\fR
CAA records.
.TP 10n
\fBsnoop\fR
Perform cache snooping against all NS servers for a given domain, testing all with file containing the domains, file given with \-D option.
.TP 10n
\fBtld\fR
Remove the TLD of given domain and test against all TLDs registered in IANA.
.TP 10n
\fBzonewalk\fR
Perform a DNSSEC zone walk using NSEC records.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Standard enumeration of a domain:
.B dnsrecon \-d example.com
.TP
Attempt a zone transfer (AXFR) against all name servers of zonetransfer.me:
.B dnsrecon \-t axfr \-d zonetransfer.me
.TP
Brute force subdomains with a wordlist, saving the results as JSON:
.B dnsrecon \-t brt \-d example.com \-D /path/to/wordlist.txt \-j results.json
.TP
Reverse lookup of a CIDR range:
.B dnsrecon \-t rvl \-r 192.0.2.0/24
.TP
Standard enumeration plus crt.sh, SPF and WHOIS expansion through Shodan:
.B dnsrecon \-d example.com \-k \-s \-w \-\-shodan
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHODAN_API_KEY
Shodan API key used by
.B \-\-shodan
when
.B \-\-shodan\-key
is not given.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/dnsrecon/dnsrecon.log
Log file, rotated at 100 MB.
.TP
.I /etc/dnsrecon/namelist.txt
Wordlist used for
.B brt
and
.B snoop
when
.B \-D
is not given. If it does not exist, the
.I namelist.txt
bundled with the Python package is used.
